From 99012f0c9192e067a5780f5ca998fc9756257b9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kmsreddy@maxlinear.com" <kmsreddy@lvdocker8.lvsw.maxlinear.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 08:13:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-86390 Fix WPS UUID not updating on BSS reload

**Issue:**
WPS UUID configured via pwhm/ubus was not reflected in probe response
frames after BSS reload. Probe responses continued to advertise the old
MAC-based UUID (4e4e634e-5750-fe4e-fe4f-524e4e4e634e) instead of the
configured UUID (8a57d731-a5fd-4028-88a4-02855145d572).

**RCA:**
When pwhm updates WPS configuration and triggers RELOAD_BSS command,
hostapd reloads the configuration file and calls hostapd_reload_bss()
which invokes hostapd_update_wps() to refresh WPS parameters. While
hostapd_init_wps() (used during initial startup) correctly copies UUID
from conf->uuid to wps->uuid, hostapd_update_wps() (used during reload)
was missing this UUID copy logic. This caused the WPS context to retain
the old UUID value even though conf->uuid was updated from the reloaded
configuration file.

**FIX:**
Added UUID copy logic in hostapd_update_wps() to synchronize UUID from
configuration to WPS context during BSS reload:
- src/ap/wps_hostapd.c: Added UUID update in hostapd_update_wps()
      os_memcpy(wps->uuid, conf->uuid, UUID_LEN);
---
 src/ap/wps_hostapd.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/wps_hostapd.c b/src/ap/wps_hostapd.c
index 8ca265d15..190037666 100644
--- a/src/ap/wps_hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/wps_hostapd.c
@@ -1572,6 +1572,12 @@ void hostapd_update_wps(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 		wps->psk_set = 1;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_VENDOR_MXL
+	/* Update UUID if configured */
+	if (!is_nil_uuid(conf->uuid))
+		os_memcpy(wps->uuid, conf->uuid, UUID_LEN);
+#endif /* CONFIG_VENDOR_MXL */
+
 	hostapd_wps_update_multi_ap(hapd, wps->registrar);
 
 	hostapd_wps_set_vendor_ext(hapd, wps);
-- 
2.43.0

